[2026-10-13T19:06:26.187Z] [ASSISTANT] Done. Here's the answer to your question and what changed.

## Why you saw a Fedora logo

Not a misconfigured theme. Plymouth was correctly set to `Theme=openqos` — including in the initramfs. But **the OpenQOS theme was never in the initramfs**:

| Check | Before |
| --- | --- |
| `plymouthd.conf` in the initramfs | `Theme=openqos` |
| `openqos` theme files in the initramfs | **0 entries** |
| Themes actually in the initramfs | `bgrt`, `details`, `spinner`, `text` |
| `/usr/share/pixmaps/system-logo-white.png` in the initramfs | Fedora's, 9523 bytes |

Two stages draw your boot screen. The first runs Plymouth out of the initramfs, and it was told to load a theme that wasn't there, so it fell back to the bundled `spinner` theme — whose watermark is the Fedora logo. Compounding it, dracut copies `system-logo-white.png` into the initramfs **unconditionally** (`test -e ... && inst_simple`), so the fallback artwork was hard-coded to Fedora's. VirtualBox presents no BGRT, so it always took that path.

## What changed

- `kiwi/openqos/base.xml` — excludes `fedora-logos`, `generic-logos`, `plymouth-theme-spinner`, `plymouth-system-theme`.
- `packages/openqos-branding` — ships `/usr/share/pixmaps/system-logo-white.png` (our mark) and a dracut snippet; declares `Provides: system-logos`.
- `branding/dracut/50-openqos-plymouth.conf` — new; pins the theme **and everything it needs to draw** into the initramfs.
- `kiwi/openqos/kde.xml` — names `plymouth-plugin-two-step`; corrected a stale claim.
- `packages/openqos-release` — owns the `/etc/os-release` symlink.

Two of those came from things that went wrong and taught me the real shape of the problem:

**The first rebuild failed**, loudly: excluding `fedora-logos` didn't remove the file, it let dnf substitute `generic-logos`, which owns the identical path. The repo's own comment said that package "cannot be removed" — that was simply wrong. `breeze-icon-theme` and friends require the *virtual* name `system-logos`, not the package. Both providers are excluded now and `openqos-branding` provides the name.

**The second rebuild succeeded but was still broken.** Excluding `plymouth-theme-spinner` silently removed `two-step.so` — the module *our* theme declares — because that theme required it at an exact version and dracut had been installing it as a side effect. The theme would have shipped present-but-unloadable. The snippet now names the plugin, `label-freetype.so`, both renderers, and `libply-splash-graphics.so.5` explicitly.

## Verified in the finished ISO

```
initramfs themes : details, openqos, text          (no bgrt, no spinner)
initramfs plugins: details.so, label-freetype.so, text.so, two-step.so
initramfs renders: drm.so, frame-buffer.so  +  libply-splash-graphics.so.5
system-logo-white: 16329 bytes  (ours; Fedora's was 9523)
live root themes : details, openqos, text, tribar  (no bgrt, no spinner)
live root pixmaps: no fedora-logo* files
```

ISO: `kiwi/build/OpenQOS-KDE-Live/OpenQOS.x86_64-44.iso`, 3,511,291,904 bytes, SHA-256 `42025eb14665f4f18031dad7844895f57242493bfd71fe673442218fe195e803`.

**One honest limit:** I verified files, not pixels. This build VM has no DRM device, so Plymouth falls back to its text renderer here — the project's own note on the theme already records that. The final visual confirmation has to be your VirtualBox boot.

## Two things I did not do

**Fedora's wallpapers.** Genuinely blocked: `f44-backgrounds-base` is required at an **exact version** by `f44-backgrounds-kde`, which `desktop-backgrounds-kde` requires, which `kde-settings-plasma`, `kde-settings-plasmalogin` and `plasma-setup` require. It can't be excluded, only replaced — needing a package that Provides and Obsoletes all three at a pin that moves every Fedora release. Same coupling `openqos-release` already documents. Least visible item, too: the default wallpaper is already OpenQOS's.

**"Fedora release 44" in `/etc/system-release`.** I started removing it, then found `docs/architecture.md
