[2026-10-13T19:39:25.996Z] [ASSISTANT] Building. The failure pattern here is worth naming, because it's recurring and I hit it twice: **Fedora ships an unbranded counterpart to each of its branded packages, and excluding only the branded one transfers the work rather than removing it.** `fedora-logos` gave way to `generic-logos` (file conflict on the shared logo path), and `fedora-release` gave way to `generic-release`, whose sole file is `/usr/lib/os-release` — the exact path `openqos-release` exists to own.

The fix is a family glob, `fedora-release*` plus `generic-release*`, in both the bootstrap and image sections. This is also why answering the requirement properly matters more than naming one package: `setup` wants `system-release`, `fedora-repos` wants `system-release(44)`, and `fedora-release-common` wants `fedora-release-identity = 44-18`, and each is a separate way for the exclusion to be quietly bypassed.
